# RevenueCat PUBLIC SDK key. `test_…` is the project's Test Store key: purchases
# complete instantly, cost nothing, and need no App Store Connect product, no
# sandbox Apple ID and no Paid Applications agreement. Store builds use the
# Apple key (`appl_…`) via `eas env:create` for production AND preview.
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=test_...

# OPTIONAL. Sentry crash reporting (org pe-yhunko, EU region). A DSN is public —
# it can only write events. Leave it blank and the SDK initialises disabled: the
# app boots and the tests pass exactly as before, it just reports nothing.
# Reporting is off in development regardless, so this only matters to a build.
#
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN is the other half and is NOT here: it is a real secret, it
# has no EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix so it never reaches the bundle, and it lives in the
# EAS environment (`eas env:create`). Without it a Release build ships with no
# uploaded source maps and every stack trace is minified garbage.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# OPTIONAL. Brand search in the add/edit form (developers.brandfetch.com — the
# client id is public by design). The endpoint answers anonymous requests today,
# so search works without this; set it anyway, because the parameter is
# documented as required and the fallback is typing a domain by hand.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BRANDFETCH_CLIENT_ID=
